BT 1 0 0 1 0 60.6 Tm 11.6 TL /F2 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Error analysis.) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( The 796 false positives look like the true positives: 93% are married-civ-spouse, about 45 years old,) Tj T* (working 46 hours a week, often in executive or professional jobs, with a mean predicted probability of 0.54. The 546 false) Tj T* (negatives almost never have capital gains \(29% of the true positives do\), have less education \(10.0 against 12.0 years\)) Tj T* -0.095335 Tw (and are often craft or machine-operator workers, with a mean probability of 0.19. The model leans on marital status, capital) Tj T* 0 Tw (gain and education \(permutation importance 0.067, 0.051 and 0.033\), so it over-flags married professionals and misses) Tj T* (well-paid people in trades without capital income. Cross-validation \(OOF F1 0.727\) and test \(0.728\) agree.) Tj T* ET
