BT 1 0 0 1 0 60.6 Tm 11.6 TL /F1 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (This model predicts whether a person earned more than $50K a year in the 1994 census. Its limits start with the data. The) Tj T* (labels are over thirty years old, the threshold means little today, and "high income" is partly a household quantity here,) Tj T* (because marital status and relationship are among the strongest signals. On the test set the final model reaches an F1 of) Tj T* -0.104494 Tw (0.73 for the >) Tj (50K class, but it still misses about one in four high earners \(recall 0.77\), and about three in ten of the people it) Tj T* 0 Tw (flags are wrong \(precision 0.69\). The errors are not random: the false negatives are mostly people with no capital income) Tj T* (and an ordinary profile, so the model has almost nothing to go on for them.) Tj T* ET
