BT 1 0 0 1 0 72.2 Tm /F1 9 Tf 11.6 TL (Bias is the main concern. I did not use race or sex as features, but the inspection tables show that this does not make the) Tj T* (model neutral. Marital status and relationship work as proxies for sex, and marital status was the most important feature in) Tj T* (the permutation test. Men are flagged as high earners far more often than women \(34.3% versus 11.2%\), their false) Tj T* (positive rate is more than three times higher \(14.8% versus 4.4%\), and recall is higher for men \(0.79 versus 0.65\). Part of) Tj T* (this mirrors real gaps in the 1994 labels, so the model learns and repeats historical inequality instead of anything about an) Tj T* (individual. Two of the racial groups are very small \(69 and 104 people\), so those numbers are too noisy to conclude) Tj T* (anything from.) Tj T* ET
