BT 1 0 0 1 0 60.6 Tm /F1 9 Tf 11.6 TL (I would not use this model to decide anything about real people, for example credit, hiring or benefits. Before any use, the) Tj T* (first thing I would do is a proper fairness audit on current, representative data: compare error rates across sex and race) Tj T* (with confidence intervals, test whether removing marital status and relationship narrows the gaps and what that costs in) Tj T* -0.015112 Tw (F1, and agree with the people who own the decision which kind of error is worse. The decision threshold \(0.35 here\) would) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.059835 Tw (have to be revisited with that cost in mind, since it deliberately trades precision for recall. If the audit fails, the model should) Tj T* 0 Tw (only be used for aggregate analysis, with a human making any individual decision.) Tj T* ET
