BT 1 0 0 1 0 60.6 Tm 11.6 TL /F1 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (The task is to predict whether a person in the 1994 US census earns more than $50K a year. I combined ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (adult.data) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( and) Tj T* /F3 9 Tf (adult.test) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( into 48,842 records, read ) Tj /F4 9 Tf (?) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( as missing, and made one stratified 80/20 split with random_state=42 \(39,073 train,) Tj T* (9,769 test\). The classes are imbalanced: 37,155 people earn at most $50K and 11,687 \(23.9%\) earn more. Missing values) Tj T* (appear in ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (workclass) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(2,799\), ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (occupation) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(2,809\) and ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (native-country) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(857\). In the training data, the share earning >50K is) Tj T* (44.5% for married-civ-spouse and 4.6% for never-married people, 9.4% when ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (workclass) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( is missing, and 61.8% among) Tj T* (people with a capital gain \(91.8% have none\).) Tj T* ET
