BT 1 0 0 1 0 72.2 Tm 11.6 TL /F1 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (One ) Tj /F4 9 Tf (ColumnTransformer) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( inside a ) Tj /F4 9 Tf (Pipeline) Tj /F1 9 Tf (, so every statistic is fitted on the training part of each CV fold only.) Tj T* /F2 9 Tf (Numeric) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(age, education-num, hours-per-week, capital-gain, capital-loss\): median imputation, then standard scaling for) Tj T* (logistic regression only. ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Categorical) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(workclass, marital-status, occupation, relationship\): constant 'Unknown' imputation,) Tj T* (because missingness is informative, then one-hot encoding. ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Dropped:) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (fnlwgt) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(survey weight\), ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (education) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(duplicates) Tj T* (education-num\), ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (race) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( and ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (sex) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(excluded as model inputs, see the fairness section\), and ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (native-country) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(CV F1 0.656) Tj T* (against 0.657 with it, half the columns, and a proxy for national origin\). A log transform of the capital columns lowered) Tj T* (logistic-regression F1 \(0.645 against 0.657\), so they stay raw.) Tj T* ET
